{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1495614716,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMzA5NjAyNjg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1529","origin":"github"},"title":"`subdatasets` needs mode to query only a subset of the subdatasets","message":"At present we can only ask for all, and for all + recursive. In a dataset with many sub-subdatasets it could be very costly to ask for everything, if we already know that we only need a particular subset.\n\nFirst use-case that comes to mind is `Dataset.get_containing_subdataset()` which _repeatedly_ asks for the list of all subdatasets with recursion, only to perform a few path string check on the results. This function is presently used in `get`, `aggregate-metadata`, and `Interface._prep()`, so it would likely be quite noticeable to speed this up.","files":null}]}